      "content": "i see what u mean about the critiques. but for the sake of the paper, i want to make sure i'm not misrepresenting their side. some of these proponents argue that even if you control for things like income or education, a gap still persists in certain datasets. they claim this \"residual\" gap is the actual indicator of a biological component. can you explain the logic they use to argue that these statistical residuals are proof of genetic factors rather than just unmeasured environmental variables?",
